Z||000000||VAROOM||11-10-1999||11:38 PM||||I have a 87 GT. have replaced the top end gasketts, plugs, wires, modual, P/U coil. I have done all kinds of stuff, even tiimed it over four times, as close as you can get. The thing runs at idle just fine, try to drive it, and it acts as if it wants to die. I mean like nothing but bogg down sppit choke etc. Any help would be great, I'm getting realy frustrated!!!!!  thanks again ||||reg||9
Z||000001||DJRice||11-11-1999||10:16 AM||||Did you put the car in diagnostic mode when you retimed it?  Usually this needs to be done so the computer can properly readjust the timing.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||dogtired||11-11-1999||11:09 AM||||Would look at everything you have done so far? It is relative easy to mix up plug wires especially on the firewall side? Then re check timing. All that being done and if still having problem check your exhaust. On my 87SE V6 right after a total rebuild the motor sounded sweet under no load but wouldn't pull the car worth a spit. The Catalytic Converter had come apart on the inside and plugged the exhaust, therefore no power. Didn't really have the choke-sputter just no power?<BR>You might check all your vacuum lines if one or some are unhooked these little motors really SUCK??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Good luck||||reg||10
